{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence0A13RelationCodecO","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxRelationCodec","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"enum","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxRelationCodec"}],"title":"SwiduxRelationCodec"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Type Methods","anchor":"Type-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec\/reconcile(_:with:in:)-1wwve","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec\/reconcile(_:with:in:)-5oivn"],"generated":true}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/swiduxrelationcodec"]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reconciles a generated model’s "},{"code":"@Relation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" properties against the domain"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value being written. Not meant to be called directly."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxRelationCodec","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Why-a-converter-cant-just-rebuild-its-children","text":"Why a converter can’t just rebuild its children"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The obvious ","type":"text"},{"code":"update(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" body — ","type":"text"},{"code":"self.chapters = try domain.chapters.map { try ChapterModel(from: $0) }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — is a row leak. A relationship’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"deleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fires when the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"parent"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is deleted, never when a child is dropped from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relationship, so the previously-related rows are detached rather than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"removed: they stay in the store with no owner, and nothing ever collects","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them. Every save of the parent leaves another full copy of its children","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"behind, the store grows for the life of the app, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"toDomain()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only walks the current relationship — shows nothing wrong.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So the write-back reconciles by ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead: rows whose identity survives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are updated in place, new identities are inserted, and identities that are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gone are deleted outright.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Identity-not-row-identity","text":"Identity, not row identity"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reconciling in place also keeps ","type":"text"},{"code":"persistentModelID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stable across a save.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"That matters beyond tidiness: a rebuilt child is a delete plus an insert, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under CloudKit mirroring every parent edit re-uploads its whole subtree, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every one of those writes a history transaction that a remote-change tick","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then has to resolve.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Duplicates-are-kept-as-everywhere-else","text":"Duplicates are kept, as everywhere else"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" emits no ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Attribute(.unique)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (CloudKit forbids unique","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constraints), so several related rows may legitimately share one identity.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are all updated and all kept, matching ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": converging every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matching row is safe, while picking one survivor is not — two devices pick","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"different rows, each tombstones the other’s, and both are lost.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/SwiduxRelationCodec":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxRelationCodec"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/swiduxrelationcodec","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxRelationCodec"}],"title":"SwiduxRelationCodec","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Reconciles a generated model’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Relation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" properties against the domain","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value being writt